===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|official paper}} An original or official paper used as the basis, proof, or support of anything else, including any writing, book, or other instrument conveying information pertinent to such proof or support.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1794|author=William Paley|title=View of the Evidences of Christianity|passage=Saint Luke {{...}} collected them from such '''documents''' and testimonies as he {{...}} judged to be authentic.}}
# {{senseid|en|written information}} Any material substance on which the information is represented by writing.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|year_published=2000|author={{w|Robert Lacey}}; Danny Danziger|title=The Year 1000: What life was like at the turn of The First Millennium|publisher=Abacus|location=London|page=122|passage=If a morsel of food fell off your plate, the advice of one contemporary '''document''' was to pick it up, make the sign of the cross over it, season it well - and then eat it.}}
# {{senseid|en|computing}} {{lb|en|computing}} A [[file]] that contains [[text]].
#* {{quote-book|en|editor=Julie A. Jacko|title=Human Computer Interaction Handbook|edition=3rd|year=2012|publisher=CRC Press|page=571|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=dVrRBQAAQBAJ&pg=PA571&dq=%22transclude%22&hl=&cd=2&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22transclude%22&f=false|isbn=978-1-4398-2944-8|passage=That exception is the HTML &lt;IMG&gt; tag–which transcludes an image into the context of the '''document'''. The image itself is neither embedded within the '''document''' nor copied—it is transcluded.}}
# {{senseid|en|information science}} {{lb|en|information science}} An [[object]] conveying information by whatever means, capable of being [[index]]ed alongside other similar objects.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=15 July 2022|author=Alex Urban|title=Mementos from digital worlds: Video game photography as documentation|journal=w:Journal of Documentation|doi=10.1108/JD-01-2022-0028|issn=0022-0418|section=Abstract|text=This study examines video game photography as a documentary practice. {{...}} The three themes from this study's findings – that video game photographs act as (1) vehicles for storytelling, (2) creative trophies, and (3) aesthetic tokens – reveal how personally meaningful '''documents''' emerge from this medium.}}
# {{senseid|en|precept}} {{lb|en|obsolete}} That which is taught or authoritatively set forth; precept; instruction; dogma.
#* {{RQ:Watts Improvement|passage=And particularly they should take care that the memory of the learner be not too much crowded with a tumultuous heap or overbearing multitude of '''documents''' or ideas at one time.}}
# {{senseid|en|example}} {{lb|en|obsolete}} An example for instruction or warning.
#* {{RQ:Raleigh Historie of the World|passage=They were forthwith stoned to death, as a '''document''' to others.}}

