#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|author=Louise J. Wilkinson|title=Women in Thirteenth-Century Lincolnshire|page=92|passage=Significantly, on '''documenting''' Thomas's subsequent outlawry and Margery's waivery, the court clerk recorded that it was not known whether they had any chattels because they were strangers.}}
